From: Bluejay postmarketOS port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: gs101: mark GPU DMA coherent

The GS101 GPU is integrated coherently and advertises ACE-Lite through
GPU_COHERENCY_FEATURES.  Without dma-coherent, panfrost selects
COHERENCY_NONE, while Mesa and the GPU exchange job descriptors and shader
memory through a path intended to be coherent.  Match the newer GS101 tree
and describe the integration correctly.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
@@ -1848,6 +1848,7 @@
 			interrupt-names = "job", "mmu", "gpu";
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 420 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
 				     <GIC_SPI 421 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
 				     <GIC_SPI 419 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			dma-coherent;
 		};
 	};
 
